  "name": "Hanko",
  "abstract": "Open-source authentication and user management built around passkeys, with passwords, email passcodes, TOTP and security-key MFA, social sign-in and SAML enterprise SSO. Authentication runs through a flow API, embedded Hanko Elements web components and a frontend SDK, with session JWTs verified by your backend through a JWKS endpoint. It is not an OpenID Provider: it consumes OIDC and SAML identity providers and issues its own tokens. Webhooks, custom JWT claims, an Admin API, and organizations with roles cover integration. Available as Hanko Cloud (Starter, Pro and Enterprise plans, hosted in Germany) or self-hosted under AGPL-3.0, with the frontend packages under MIT.",
